   Properties: {'session_id': 'a9a974d2-6b6d-4fd6-8622-1e397c3cf05d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.3876276392501856, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://odphp.health.gov/healthypeople/priority-areas/health-literacy-healthy-people-2030', 'https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.06389081865130358, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation posits that health literacy leads to a healthy lifestyle solely through the internalization of societal norms and the desire to conform to external pressures, regardless of personal beliefs or intrinsic motivation. This is a narrow and somewhat flawed causal pathway. Health literacy can influence healthy lifestyle choices through various mechanisms, such as increased knowledge, self-efficacy, and motivation, not just conformity to social norms. By asserting that the relationship holds \\"regardless of an individual\\u2019s personal beliefs or intrinsic motivation\\" and that the \\"primary driver\\" is external pressure, the explanation overlooks other plausible and internally logical pathways. Thus, the reasoning is incomplete and somewhat internally inconsistent.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7697268324666807, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6879984700377219, 'motivation': 'Health literacy causes a healthy lifestyle through a process of cognitive reinforcement, whereby individuals who possess high levels of health literacy internalize societal norms and expectations regarding health behaviors. As individuals become more health literate, they are more likely to adopt a healthy lifestyle in order to conform to perceived social standards and avoid negative evaluations from peers and community members. This direct 