1055. Size of social network-[POSITIVE]->Accessibility of information
   Properties: {'session_id': 'a9a974d2-6b6d-4fd6-8622-1e397c3cf05d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.76915810680979, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3282379/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2799303/', 'https://www.apu.apus.edu/area-of-study/business-and-management/resources/how-social-media-sites-affect-society/', 'https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2006875117', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0747563224001031'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10066376706675818, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation asserts that a larger social network increases accessibility of information by enhancing cognitive abilities through complex social interactions. However, this reasoning conflates two distinct mechanisms: (1) direct access to more information sources via a larger social network, and (2) indirect cognitive improvements leading to better information accessibility. The explanation dismisses the direct pathway (actual channels or sources) and relies entirely on cognitive enhancement, which is not sufficiently justified as the primary or sole mechanism. The logic that cognitive stimulation from larger networks alone would improve information accessibility, regardless of actual information sources, is not fully sound or clearly established within the explanation itself.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7516300615964692, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6295920030189582, 'motivation': 'Size of social network causes accessibility of information to increase by enhancing individuals’ cognitive processing abilities. As the size of social network expands, individuals are exposed to more complex social interactions, which purportedly strengthens their cognitive capacities. This cognitive enhancem