103. Acute care demand leading to an ED visit-[POSITIVE]->Financial resources
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2056268825807455, 'original_motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit causes financial resources to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Increased demand for acute care through ED visits requires more financial expenditures from the healthcare system, thus reducing available financial resources. Conversely, if acute care demand leading to ED visits decreases, fewer financial resources are expended.', 'session_id': '372c60ba-d159-4c37-9fd2-0dd5978c3ddd', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8599001852861998, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09902712177878471, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation logically connects an increase in acute care demand (resulting in more ED visits) to an increase in financial resources for hospitals. The reasoning is that each additional ED visit provides an opportunity for billing and revenue generation (e.g., insurance reimbursement), which can, in turn, increase the hospital\'s financial resources. The explanation also states that higher patient throughput enables hospitals to maximize operational budgets and invest in staff and infrastructure, implying that increased revenue translates to more available resources."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.5938018894440998, 'motivation': 'An increase in acute care demand that leads to more ED visits can actually boost financial resources for hospitals because each visit generates billing opportunities and revenue from insurance reimbursements. This higher patient throughput allows healthcare facilities to maximize their operational budgets and invest more in staff and infrastructure. Thus, more ED visits can directly contribute to greater financial resources.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in acute care demand that leads to more ED visits can actually boost financial resources for hospitals because each visit generates billing opportunities and revenue from insurance reimbursements. This higher patient throughput allows healthcare facilities to maximize their operational budgets and invest more in staff and infrastructure. Thus, more ED visits can directly contribute to greater financial resources.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0061568503822615325, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6700034327701844, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 7.402000878794971e-06, 'judge_prob_std': 0.314685750835313}

