514. Financial resources-[POSITIVE]->Education level
   Properties: {'session_id': '372c60ba-d159-4c37-9fd2-0dd5978c3ddd', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6595847994752642, 'citations': ['https://www.stlouisfed.org/publications/page-one-economics/2017/01/03/education-income-and-wealth', 'https://www.nea.org/resource-library/financial-literacy-economic-inequality', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/education/articles/10.3389/feduc.2024.1397060/full', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5450829/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09679309517866667, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The given explanation claims that a higher education level leads to an increase in financial resources, citing superior financial acumen and increased capacity for financial management and investment as mechanisms. However, the source and target variables are reversed in the explanation: the prompt asks for the effect of financial resources on education level, but the explanation describes the effect of education level on financial resources. The logical structure of the explanation is internally consistent for the direction it describes (education \\u2192 financial resources), but it does not address the relationship as posed (financial resources \\u2192 education). Thus, while the causal reasoning within the explanation is coherent for the reversed direction, it fails to provide the required reasoning for the stated relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7938868562977494, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.634164213990295, 'motivation': 'A higher education level directly leads to an increase in financial resources, as individuals with advanced education are presumed to possess superior financial acumen and are more likely to accumulate wealth. This enhanced capacity for financial management and investment, attributed to higher education level, results in the gradual