654. Healthy lifestyle-[NEGATIVE]->Chronic addiction
   Properties: {'session_id': '372c60ba-d159-4c37-9fd2-0dd5978c3ddd', 'judge_perplexity': 3.201263731231582e+16, 'citations': ['https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002149.htm', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10557909718486322, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Step 1: The explanation claims that a healthy lifestyle decreases chronic addiction by increasing willpower and discipline, which then \\"directly immunizes\\" individuals against neurobiological changes from addiction. This presents a direct, deterministic mechanism.  \\nStep 2: It further asserts that regular exercise and nutrition make the body \\"physically resistant\\" and that it is \\"biologically impossible\\" for addiction to take hold in such individuals.  \\nStep 3: The explanation also claims that a decline in healthy lifestyle leads directly to physiological vulnerability, making addiction more likely.  \\nStep 4: There is a conflation of behavioral/psychological factors (willpower, discipline) with strong biological determinism (immunity, impossibility), and a claim of a \\"protective biological barrier\\" that ensures a direct inverse relationship.  \\nStep 5: The logic overstates the mechanisms: While healthy lifestyle factors can contribute to lower risk of addiction (e.g., via improved coping skills, social support, brain health), the claim that these factors create biological immunity or make addiction biologically impossible is not logically sound.  \\nStep 6: The explanation leaps from reasonable behavioral associations to absolute biological determinism, which is an unsupported and illogical jump internally."}], "aggregate_scor