ctly increases the likelihood of developing a 24/7-care mentality, as the neurological changes in the brain promote an obsessive focus on caregiving routines. This means that individuals with cognitive disorders are more likely to believe that round-the-clock care is always necessary, regardless of their actual needs.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.013846382474381481, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7136444516731502, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0040712538269802225, 'judge_prob_std': 0.30765810036560876}

