ads to increased investments and funding opportunities, which in turn further elevate capacity. Therefore, the initial availability of financial resources directly stimulates a cycle of capacity growth by signaling organizational potential to external stakeholders.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.012739849780534628, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8461069211302317, 'min_prob': 0.1337118998394874, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7443491694829633, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0027210982418902794, 'prob_variance': 0.059540743476725895, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0018896031491775992, 'judge_prob_std': 0.316031950635509, 'avg_nll': 0.24148717774027176, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2404351529161635, 'original_motivation': 'Financial resources cause capacity to increase in a direct causal relationship. Increasing financial resources enables the acquisition of personnel, equipment, and infrastructure, directly expanding capacity. Conversely, reducing financial resources constrains the ability to maintain or grow capacity.', 'prob_std': 0.24400972004558732, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.2731411302666247, 'max_window_entropy': 0.8486219151640353}

