   Properties: {'session_id': '8fba4771-8baa-4773-85c8-a3776f87d6d7', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7225383501067775, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4131737/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09073392640499485, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a somewhat plausible mechanism (improved professional functioning leads to more efficient procedures, enhancing patient understanding), and maintains correct temporality (cause precedes effect and avoids reverse causation). However, the specific causal pathway is vague\\u2014how streamlined processes inherently foster health literacy is not clearly articulated. The explanation also overstates the strength of the relationship without substantiating why this influence is substantial, and it claims the effect is \\"independent of explicit educational efforts,\\" which is not internally justified. Overall, it is internally consistent but lacks sufficient detail and justification on mechanism and strength."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7529743721157138, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6342280003212367, 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes changes in health literacy because enhanced professional functioning leads to more efficient diagnostic procedures and treatment protocols, which directly result in improved patient understanding of their health conditions and necessary self-care behaviors. As healthcare professionals function more effectively, the streamlined clinical processes themselves inherently foster greater health literacy among patients, independent of explicit educational efforts or communication strategies.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'spurious_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes changes in health literacy because enhanced professional functioning leads to more efficient diagnostic procedures and treatment protocols, which directly result in improved patient understanding of their health conditions and necessary self-care behaviors. As healthcare professionals function more effectively, the streamlined clinical processes themselves inherently foster greater health literacy among patients, independent of explicit educational efforts or communication strategies.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.008555577942779861, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8180348674733325, 'min_prob': 0.053479976733057426, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7109998628847615, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004556913364972298, 'prob_variance': 0.0676737294735244, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0022120404335798814, 'judge_prob_std': 0.30122072705077063, 'avg_nll': 0.29262922428686644, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3329218467964823, 'original_motivation': "Functioning of healthcare professionals causes health literacy to change in a direct causal relationship. When healthcare professionals function effectively, they are better able to communicate, educate, and empower patients, directly increasing patients' health literacy. Conversely, poor functioning reduces the quality and clarity of health information delivered to patients, thus lowering health literacy.", 'prob_std': 0.2601417488092298, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.3399458789271959, 'max_window_entropy': 1.12386927951278}

580. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Care avoidance behavior
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.176663647577681, 'original_motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where functioning of healthcare professionals causes care avoidance behavior or vice versa. Any potential influence is likely mediated by other variables such as accessibility of information, feelings of fear and shame, or organizational structure, which are already present in the CLD. Including a direct link would misrepresent the causal mechanisms involved. Therefore, no direct causality exists between these two variables.', 'session_id': '8fba4771-8baa-4773-85c8-a3776f87d6d7', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8116716801241355, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10640637373310666, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a specific causal mechanism (patients feeling intimidated or unworthy), which addresses plausibility, and it maintains correct temporal ordering (functioning precedes avoidance) and direction. However, the strength of the relationship is not clearly conveyed\\u2014it does not establish that this is a substantial or non-trivial influence, and the reasoning, while plausible, may lack internal coherence as it assumes that higher professional functioning generally leads to intimidation rather than reassurance, which could be seen as an overgeneralization. Thus, it meets some but not all criteria."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6085465417162406, 'motivation': 'An increase in the functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes more care avoidance behavior among patients, because when professionals are highly efficient and skilled, patients may feel intimidated or unworthy of care. This leads them to avoid seeking medical help altogether, believing only the most severe cases deserve attention from such competent staff.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in the functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes more care avoidance behavior among patients, because when professionals are highly efficient and skilled, patients may feel intimidated or unworthy of care. This leads them to avoid seeking medical help altogether, believing only the most severe cases deserve attention from such competent staff.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.04297124156494016, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6847756066827592, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.002901823522869404, 'judge_prob_std': 0.32619989842596003}

