   Properties: {'session_id': '8fba4771-8baa-4773-85c8-a3776f87d6d7', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6622954018549245, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8390337/', 'https://psychiatryonline.org/doi/10.1176/appi.ps.201400351', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9490697/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK44249/', 'https://www.nami.org/your-journey/identity-and-cultural-dimensions/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0947606511188261, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a plausible and specific causal mechanism (PLAUDIBILITY) by describing how cognitive demands from language and cultural barriers may lead to neural fatigue and reduced psychological reserve, which could plausibly contribute to mental disorder. TEMPORALITY is addressed, as the sequence is clear (barriers precede mental disorder) and reverse causation is not suggested. However, the STRENGTH of the effect is not convincingly established; while the mechanism is described in detail, it is unclear whether this is more than a minor or rare pathway, and the language is somewhat speculative. COHERENCE is mostly maintained, but there is a minor inconsistency in asserting both enhanced resilience and simultaneous depletion without clarifying how these co-occur. Thus, the explanation meets two criteria well, but is notably weak on strength and has slight coherence issues."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7977666799336678, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6465042094871359, 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers directly enhance cognitive resilience, as individuals facing these challenges regularly adapt to new environments and linguistic contexts. This heightened adaptability leads to increased mental stimulation and problem-solving, which in turn can overtax mental processing