idity often leads to increased medical supervision and more frequent doctor visits, which ensures that patients receive better guidance on medication use. As a result, individuals with multiple chronic conditions are less likely to use their medications incorrectly compared to those with fewer health issues.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7249620683565113, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.004851327294431056, 'judge_prob_std': 0.307152114408401}

